{
  "email": "sofia.rossi@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender asks about automated laptop check-in alert after two weeks of leave. Need account status and assigned devices per KB-018."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0107",
  "reason": "Check online state, last check-in, and warnings for the user's assigned laptop per KB-018."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, welcome back. It isn't a serious problem, but the alert is valid: your laptop (BL-LT-0107) has not checked in for about 12 days, which is why it was flagged. Updates and security policies can't reach it until it checks in. Please do the following when you can: 1) Power on the laptop and connect it to the internet (office Wi-Fi, home Wi-Fi, or a wired connection). 2) Keep it signed in and leave it on for about 30 minutes. 3) Restart the laptop. Once that's done, reply to this ticket and let us know. If it still shows as offline after the restart, we'll take a closer look. If the laptop won't turn on or connect to the internet, tell us what you see on the screen.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: Sofia Rossi (user 7), Marketing, account active, not blocked, no failed logins, VPN enabled. Assigned device BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11 Pro), offline, last check-in 2026-09-29 02:54 UTC, warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Per KB-018 (>7 days needs follow-up), asked the user to power on, connect, stay signed in 30 min, and restart. Escalate under KB-018 if device comes online but still doesn't check in after restart, or if the user cannot locate the device (KB-021). Next step: re-run check_device_status after user reports back. No account actions taken. Note: device check-in is ~12 days old; the user was on leave, so this is likely a benign powered-off laptop, not a loss.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-018"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
